    "headline": "CoStar Stock Slumps After Earnings Beat on Lower Revenue Expectations",
    "summary": "CoStar Group  adjusted earnings beat analyst expectations—but a slight revenue miss and the company’s lower revenue estimate for the full year  dragged the stock lower in after hours trading.  CoStar  a real estate information technology company, on Tuesday reported non-GAAP earnings of 32 cents on $925 million in revenue.  Earnings beat analyst estimates that called for 29 cents a share, while revenue was a touch below the roughly $929 million expected, according to FactSet.",
